\s1 The LORD’s Promise
\p \v 19 \w Therefore|strong="H03651"\w* \w this is what|strong="H03541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w says|strong="H00559"\w*:
\b 
\q1 “\w If|strong="H00518"\w* \w you return|strong="H07725"\w*, \w I will restore you|strong="H07725"\w*;
\q2 \w you will stand|strong="H05975"\w* \w in My presence|strong="H06440"\w*.
\q1 \w And if|strong="H00518"\w* \w you speak|strong="H03318"\w* \w words that are noble|strong="H03368"\w* \w instead of worthless|strong="H02151"\w*,
\q2 \w you will be|strong="H01961"\w* \w My spokesman|strong="H06310"\w*.
\q1 \w It is they|strong="H01992"\w* \w who must turn|strong="H07725"\w* \w to you|strong="H00413"\w*,
