\p \v 7 \w So they entered|strong="H00935"\w* \w the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w* \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w they did not|strong="H03808"\w* \w obey|strong="H08085"\w* \w the voice|strong="H06963"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w*, \w and they went|strong="H00935"\w* \w as far as|strong="H05704"\w* \w Tahpanhes|strong="H08471"\w*.
\p \v 8 \w Then the word|strong="H01697"\w* \w of the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w came|strong="H01961"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H03414"\w* \w at Tahpanhes|strong="H08471"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w*: \v 9 “\w In the sight|strong="H05869"\w* \w vvv|strong="H00582"\w* \w [of the] Jews|strong="H03064"\w*, \w pick up|strong="H03947"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03027"\w* \w some large|strong="H01419"\w* \w stones|strong="H00068"\w* \w and bury them|strong="H02934"\w* \w in the clay|strong="H04423"\w* \w of the brick pavement|strong="H04404"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w at the entrance|strong="H06607"\w* \w to Pharaoh’s|strong="H06547"\w* \w palace|strong="H01004"\w* \w at Tahpanhes|strong="H08471"\w*.
\p \v 10 \w Then tell them|strong="H00559"\w* \w that|strong="H00413"\w* \w this is what|strong="H03541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*, \w the God|strong="H00430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H02005"\w* \w says|strong="H00559"\w*: ‘\w I will send for|strong="H07971"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03947"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w My servant|strong="H05650"\w* \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H05019"\w* \w king|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H00894"\w*, \w and I will set|strong="H07760"\w* \w his throne|strong="H03678"\w* \w over|strong="H04605"\w* \w these|strong="H00428"\w* \w stones|strong="H00068"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w I have embedded|strong="H02934"\w*, \w and he will spread|strong="H05186"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w his royal pavilion|strong="H08237"\w* \w over them|strong="H05921"\w*. \v 11 \w He will come|strong="H00935"\w* \w and strike down|strong="H05221"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w*, \w bringing death|strong="H04194"\w* \w to those|strong="H00834"\w* \w destined for death|strong="H04194"\w*, \w captivity|strong="H07628"\w* \w to those|strong="H00834"\w* \w destined for captivity|strong="H07628"\w*, \w and the sword|strong="H02719"\w* \w to those|strong="H00834"\w* \w destined for the sword|strong="H02719"\w*.
\p \v 12 \w I will kindle|strong="H03341"\w* \w a fire|strong="H00784"\w* \w in the temples|strong="H01004"\w* \w of the gods|strong="H00430"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w*, \w and [Nebuchadnezzar] will burn [those temples]|strong="H08313"\w* \w and take [their gods] as captives|strong="H07617"\w*.\f + \fr 43:12 \ft Literally \fqa and he will burn them and take them captive\f* \w So he will wrap himself|strong="H05844"\w* \w with|strong="H00853"\w* \w the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w* \w as|strong="H00834"\w* \w a shepherd|strong="H07462"\w* \w wraps himself|strong="H05844"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w in his garment|strong="H00899"\w*, \w and he will depart|strong="H03318"\w* \w from there|strong="H08033"\w* \w unscathed|strong="H07965"\w*. \v 13 \w He will demolish|strong="H07665"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the sacred pillars|strong="H04676"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01053"\w* \w of the temple of the sun|strong="H01053"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w in the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w*,\f + \fr 43:13 \ft LXX \fqa He will demolish the pillars of Heliopolis in On \ft or \fqa He will demolish the pillars of Heliopolis in Egypt\ft ; Hebrew \fqa He will demolish the pillars of Beth-shemesh in the land of Egypt\f* \w and|strong="H00853"\w* \w he will burn down|strong="H08313"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00784"\w* \w the temples|strong="H01004"\w* \w of the gods|strong="H00430"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w*.’”
\c 44
\s1 Judgment on the Jews in Egypt
\p \v 1 \w This is the word|strong="H01697"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w came|strong="H01961"\w* \w to|strong="H00413"\w* \w Jeremiah|strong="H03414"\w* \w concerning|strong="H00413"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the Jews|strong="H03064"\w* \w living|strong="H03427"\w* \w in the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of Egypt|strong="H04714"\w*\f + \fr 44:1 \ft Or \fqa Lower Egypt \ft or \fqa northern Egypt\ft ; also in verse 15\f*— \w . . .|strong="H03427"\w* \w in Migdol|strong="H04024"\w*, \w Tahpanhes|strong="H08471"\w*, \w and Memphis|strong="H05297"\w*\f + \fr 44:1 \ft LXX; Hebrew \fqa Noph\f*— \w and in the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of Pathros|strong="H06624"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00559"\w*:\f + \fr 44:1 \ft Or \fqa Upper Egypt \ft or \fqa southern Egypt\ft ; also in verse 15\f* \v 2 “\w This is what|strong="H03541"\w* \w the LORD|strong="H03068"\w* \w of Hosts|strong="H06635"\w*, \w the God|strong="H00430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w says|strong="H00559"\w*: \w You|strong="H00859"\w* \w have seen|strong="H07200"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the disaster|strong="H07451"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w I brought|strong="H00935"\w* \w against|strong="H05921"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05921"\w* \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w the cities|strong="H05892"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H03063"\w*; \w and behold|strong="H02005"\w*, \w they lie today in ruins|strong="H02723"\w* \w . . .|strong="H03117"\w* \w and|strong="H02088"\w* \w desolation|strong="H00369"\w* . . . \w . . .|strong="H03427"\w* \v 3 \w because of|strong="H06440"\w* \w the evil|strong="H07451"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w they have done|strong="H06213"\w*.
\p \w They provoked Me to anger|strong="H03707"\w* \w by continuing|strong="H01980"\w* \w to burn incense|strong="H06999"\w* \w [and] to serve|strong="H05647"\w* \w other|strong="H00312"\w* \w -|strong="H00834"\w* \w gods|strong="H00430"\w* \w that neither|strong="H03808"\w* \w they|strong="H01992"\w* \w [nor] you|strong="H00859"\w* \w nor your fathers|strong="H00001"\w* \w ever knew|strong="H03045"\w*. \v 4 \w Yet I sent|strong="H07971"\w* \w you|strong="H00413"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w all|strong="H03605"\w* \w My servants|strong="H05650"\w* \w the prophets|strong="H05030"\w* \w again and again|strong="H07925"\w* \w . . .|strong="H07971"\w*,\f + \fr 44:4 \ft Literally \fqa the prophets, rising up early and sending (them),\f* \w saying|strong="H00559"\w*: ‘\w Do not|strong="H00408"\w* \w . . .|strong="H04994"\w* \w do|strong="H06213"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w this|strong="H02063"\w* \w detestable|strong="H08441"\w* \w thing|strong="H01697"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w I hate|strong="H08130"\w*.’
\p \v 5 \w But they did not|strong="H03808"\w* \w listen|strong="H08085"\w* \w or incline|strong="H05186"\w*\w . . .|strong="H00853"\w* \w their ears|strong="H00241"\w*; \w they did not|strong="H03808"\w* \w turn|strong="H07725"\w* \w from their wickedness|strong="H07451"\w* \w or stop|strong="H01115"\w* \w burning incense|strong="H06999"\w* \w to other|strong="H00312"\w* \w gods|strong="H00430"\w*. \v 6 \w Therefore My wrath|strong="H02534"\w* \w and anger|strong="H00639"\w* \w poured out|strong="H05413"\w* \w and burned|strong="H01197"\w* \w in the cities|strong="H05892"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H03063"\w* \w and in the streets|strong="H02351"\w* \w of Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w*, \w so that they have become|strong="H01961"\w* \w the desolate|strong="H02723"\w* \w ruin|strong="H08077"\w* \w they are today|strong="H03117"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02088"\w*.
