\p \v 4 \w So|strong="H01961"\w* \w in the ninth|strong="H08671"\w* \w year|strong="H08141"\w* \w of Zedekiah’s reign|strong="H04427"\w*, \w on the tenth|strong="H06218"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02320"\w* \w day of the tenth|strong="H06224"\w* \w month|strong="H02320"\w*, \w Nebuchadnezzar|strong="H05019"\w* \w king|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Babylon|strong="H00894"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01931"\w* \w marched|strong="H00935"\w* \w against|strong="H05921"\w* \w Jerusalem|strong="H03389"\w* \w with his entire|strong="H03605"\w* \w army|strong="H02428"\w*. \w They encamped|strong="H02583"\w* \w outside [the city]|strong="H05921"\w* \w and built|strong="H01129"\w* \w a siege wall|strong="H01785"\w* \w all|strong="H05439"\w* \w around it|strong="H05921"\w*. \v 5 \w And the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w was kept|strong="H00935"\w* \w under siege|strong="H04692"\w* \w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w King|strong="H04428"\w* \w Zedekiah’s|strong="H06667"\w* \w eleventh|strong="H06249"\w* \w . . .|strong="H06240"\w* \w year|strong="H08141"\w*.
